// The constants of the decimal transcendentals (dec_trans.tess), 1280 bits each, computed with mpmath at
// 1600 bits and truncated: entry k of DEC_CONSTANTS is limbs [20 k, 20 k + 20) (least significant first),
// value 2^(DEC_CONSTANT_EXP[k] - 1280) times that. The Stirling coefficients B_2k / (2k (2k - 1)) follow the
// named constants, their signs alternating (positive for k = 1).

/// The named constants' indices in DEC_CONSTANTS.
preset DEC_LN2: USize = 0  // ln 2
preset DEC_PI: USize = 1  // pi
preset DEC_LN10: USize = 2  // ln 10
preset DEC_HALF_LN_2PI: USize = 3  // ln(2 pi) / 2
preset DEC_TWO_OVER_SQRT_PI: USize = 4  // 2 / sqrt(pi)

/// The index of B_2 / 2 in DEC_CONSTANTS, and how many Stirling coefficients follow.
preset DEC_STIRLING: USize = 5
